Evidence pack, step 4 (rule out a fix). A teammate proposes this change to the handler:

existing = check(user_id, course_id)
if existing == 0:
    time.sleep(0.1)
    existing = check(user_id, course_id)   # check again, just before inserting
if existing > 0:
    return 200, {"status": "already_enrolled"}
insert(user_id, course_id)

Statement: "Running the check a second time after a short sleep, right before the INSERT, closes the race: two requests can no longer both pass the check."
